From 6335cb4da13d07377e852e24224bc4d46bfb7e5b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 13:44:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 125/240] Bugfix: translate the vertex labels of non-compact
 edge arrays and report unknown labels in `dgraphBuild3()` [report R. Perry]

When vertex labels are given, the edges to translate were taken from
the first `edgelocnbr` slots of the edge array, which is wrong when
the edge array is not compact: unused slots were translated while real
edges beyond these slots kept their labels. Moreover, an edge label
found on no process was left as is, without any error being reported.

Collect edges vertex by vertex, which also checks that the sum of
vertex degrees matches the announced number of local edges, and report
edges whose label has not been translated. Add a test program for
labeled graphs with non-compact edge arrays.

Refs: DGR-12
